# Reference capture script (#9). `yahaha capture-kit` turns it into a MIDI file for a Genos
# owner to play into ACMP, and `yahaha capture-import` plays the same script through our
# engine and compares the two. Grammar: tests/golden/README.md.
#
# Only buttons that have a MIDI Section Control message can be used here: [IntroA-D],
# [MainA-D], [Break] and [EndingA-D]. Every chord must read back as itself from the keys
# the kit plays (Fingered On Bass), and no chord is struck again while it is held (write
# "-" to hold it); src/capture.rs checks all three. The kit presses a button half a beat
# before its slot, so a button written at the start of a bar starts its fill or Break on
# the downbeat and it plays the whole bar.
# Changing this file invalidates every recording made with it, and every digest in
# tests/reference.

# Intro A, started by the first chord (Sync Start), then Main A.
[IntroA] | C | - |
# Main A: every chord type in the Data List table, one a bar, with the root moving round the
# circle of fourths so every root comes up.
| - | F6 | Bbmaj7 | Ebmaj7#11 |
| Abadd9 | Dbmaj9 | F#6(9) | Baug |
| E7#5 | Amaj7#5 | Dm | Gm6 |
| Cm7 | Fm7b5 | Bbm(add9) | Ebm9 |
| Abm11 | C#mMaj7 | F#mMaj9 | Bdim |
| Edim7 | A7 | D7sus4 | G9 |
| C7#11 | F13 | Bb7b5 | Eb7b9 |
| Ab7b13 | Db7#9 | F#sus4 | Bsus2 |
| Emaj7b5 | A(b5) | DmMaj7b5 | G1+5 |
# Main A's own fill for a whole bar, back to Main A, then a whole-bar fill into Main B.
| C1+8 | C | [MainA] F | - | [MainB] G7 |
# Main B: major and minor on all twelve roots, two chords a bar (High Key, Note Limit).
| C Db | D Eb | E F | F# G | Ab A | Bb B |
| Cm C#m | Dm Ebm | Em Fm | F#m Gm | G#m Am | Bbm Bm |
# Inversions and slash chords: with Fingered On Bass the lowest key is the bass. Some
# are written the way they read: F over G is Fadd9/G, C over Bb is C7/Bb, and Am7 over G
# (G A C E) is C6/G, Dm11 over G is F6(9)/G. The chord messages in a recording show how
# the instrument reads them.
| C/E | C/G | C6/G | D/F# | Fadd9/G | F6(9)/G | C7/Bb | Fmaj7/E |
| Am/C | G/B | Em/B | C/F# | Bbadd9/C | Eb/G | E7/G# | G7/F |
# A whole-bar Break, pressing Main C during it, so the Break leads straight into Main C.
| [Break] Am | [MainC] - |
# Main C: quick changes while notes sound (Retrigger Rule). Two, four and eight chords a
# bar, changes off the beat, and a release (the chord stays in memory).
| C F | G7 C | Am Dm7 | G7 C |
| - Am F G7 | Em A7 Dm7 G7 | Cmaj7 Fmaj7 Bm7b5 E7 | Am D7 G7 C |
| - F C F G7 C G7 C | Am E7 Am E7 Am Dm E7 Am |
| C - - F - - G7 - | C - - - Am - - - |
| Dm7 - G7 - - - C - | - - ^ - | [MainD] F |
# Main D (a style without one plays Main C after the fill): Cancel, 1+5 and 1+8 in context,
# and a chord change on the first beat of a one-beat fill.
| Am | Ccancel | - | F |
| C1+5 | F1+5 | G1+8 | C - - [MainA] G7 |
# Main A, then Ending A, left to run out. Four bars cover the longest Ending A in the kit
# (three); after a shorter one the style has stopped, which checks that it does.
| C | Dm7 - G7 [EndingA] - |
| C | - | - | - |
